    <!-- Onboarding -->
    <string name="setup_how_it_works">How Remap works</string>
    <string name="onboarding_why_title">1. Why accessibility is needed</string>
    <string name="onboarding_why_body">On Vivo, a long power press opens BlueLM by default with no native Remap option.\n\nOriginOS 6 often does not deliver KEYCODE_POWER to accessibility (Shutter keys still arrive). Viva la Circle watches for BlueLM Wake UI, dismisses it, and fires your TargetAction.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_setup_title">2. Step-by-step setup</string>
    <string name="onboarding_step_1">Tap Enable in Accessibility Settings above.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_step_2">Open Downloaded apps / Installed services.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_step_3">Select Viva la Circle.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_step_4">Turn on Use Viva la Circle and confirm.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_how_title">3. What happens on Remap</string>
    <string name="onboarding_how_body">Once enabled:\n\n• If the ROM opens BlueLM Wake UI, the service dismisses it, then fires your BlueLM TargetAction.\n• Short-press Power stays with the ROM.\n• Shutter Remap is optional under Advanced.</string>

